Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom_battmgr: default property protocol to charge units

SM8350 and SM8550 firmware reports charge capacity through individual
properties and never sends BATTMGR_BAT_INFO. Leaving the zero-initialized
unit at mWh makes CHARGE_FULL and CHARGE_FULL_DESIGN return ENODATA even
when the firmware has returned valid microamp-hour values.

Default to mAh. The SC8280XP/X1E80100 information response still replaces
this with the firmware's explicit unit before exposing capacity values.
This applies to the shared protocol, not a particular board.

--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
@@ -1646,6 +1646,9 @@ static int qcom_battmgr_probe(struct auxiliary_device *adev,
 	psy_cfg.drv_data = battmgr;
 	psy_cfg.fwnode = dev_fwnode(&adev->dev);
 
+	/* Property-based firmware reports charge; info-based firmware overrides it. */
+	battmgr->unit = QCOM_BATTMGR_UNIT_mAh;
+
 	psy_cfg_supply.drv_data = battmgr;
 	psy_cfg_supply.fwnode = dev_fwnode(&adev->dev);
 	psy_cfg_supply.supplied_to = qcom_battmgr_battery;
